// prelude unit unit (DESIGN.md sec:ir, "Identity", and step L2.8; written by
// step M0.11): how a unit, a prelude unit included, is versioned and addressed.
// The Rust-hosted checker's copy is zedc::canon::unit_address in
// crates/zedc-zir/src/canon/mod.rs.
//
// A unit has no version number. Its address is the hash of its exported
// declarations, each named and given its content address (step M0.7), so a
// changed export, or a changed local declaration an export uses, gives a new
// address, and an unused local declaration or the unit's path does not. An
// import's pin names this address; the prelude is pinned as an ordinary unit
// (step L2.8, in the package's `zed.pins`). The canonicalization VERSION is
// hashed in, so a change to the canonical form changes every address.
//
// blake3 is Zed source (row STD-blake3; a primitive only if a stage build shows
// it too slow), and the 8-byte little-endian `word` is a checker core built-in
// (step S.3); `version` is the canonicalization VERSION.

struct Export { name: String, address: Bytes }

// The argument of a program's `main` (DESIGN.md sec:ports, QUESTIONS Q51, plan row
// MAIN-args): the words after `--`, standard input, standard output, standard
// error and the environment. Each field is a port, opened only when the program
// reads it; `m.stdin` is read and `m.stdout` and `m.stderr` are pushed to. The
// Rust-hosted compiler reads it in crates/zedc-syntax/src/ast/builder.rs
// (`MAIN_INPUTS`, `MAIN_OUTPUTS`).
struct MainArgs { args: CommandLine, stdin: Lines, stdout: Lines, stderr: Lines, env: Utf8String ->? Utf8String }

unitAddress(positional exports, positional version) = {
  sorted = exports.sortBy(e -> (e.name, e.address));
  blake3(
    utf8("zed-unit\0") ++ u32le(version) ++ word(sorted.count())
      ++ sorted.foldl([], (out, e) -> out ++ word(utf8(e.name).count()) ++ utf8(e.name) ++ e.address)
  )
};
